#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Withdrawals paid from the Flutterwave balance (switchable; Paystack stays as backup).

- New payout provider "flutterwave": bank list, account name lookup, transfers
  from the Flutterwave NGN balance, status checks, balance check.
- Flutterwave webhook now also completes/refunds withdrawals (transfer.completed).
- Saved bank accounts from the Paystack days keep working (mapped automatically).
- Naira wallet funding on Flutterwave offers card, bank transfer and USSD.
- Staff alerts name the right gateway; "IP not whitelisted" refusals keep the
  customer's money held and tell staff what to fix.
- python manage.py flutterwave_payout_test  -> try ONE real small transfer first.

Nothing changes until you set DEFAULT_PROVIDER_PAYOUTS=flutterwave (withdrawals)
and DEFAULT_PROVIDER_PAYMENTS=flutterwave (wallet funding) on Render.

Unzip in the backend root (with manage.py), then:
    python3 apply_flutterwave_payouts_backend.py
    python manage.py test apps.payouts apps.payments --settings=config.settings.test
No migrations.
"""
